  "introduction": "Graphs represent numerical data pictorially, transforming raw tables into intuitive visual stories. From bar charts and histograms to time-series line graphs and the Cartesian coordinate system, this chapter develops essential skills to plot points, determine collinearity, find intercepts, and distinguish linear proportional relationships from non-linear curves.",
